SUMMARY:Experimental/Behavioural – Mehmet Yigit Gurdal (Bogazici) – A G
 raphical Representation for Binarized Scoring Rule
LOCATION:Room 304\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3053
DESCRIPTION:Mehmet Yigit Gurdal: “A Graphical Representation for Binariz
 ed Scoring Rule”\nhttps://web.bogazici.edu.tr/gurdal/\n\nZoom: https://u
 nimelb.zoom.us/j/82654401351?pwd=V6TMN2ZpNRILVKO2Y5za5S7GjfbAGG.1&from=add
 on\n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.app.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\
 nBinarized Scoring Rule (BSR) impose significant cognitive burdens on expe
 rimental subjects. We introduce a graphical representation of the BSR that
  translates its incentive structure into an intuitive visual interface\, a
 llowing subjects to observe in real time how reported beliefs map into rew
 ard probabilities. We compare this design to three alternatives: a standar
 d BSR implementation\, a No-Information treatment following Danz et al. (2
 022)\, and the Paired-Uniform Scoring Rule of Wilson and Vespa (2018). The
  graphical interface is rated as easier to understand than competing metho
 ds and yields accuracy comparable to the baseline BSR and Paired-Uniform t
 reatments\, while reducing decision time and center-pull bias. The No-Info
 rmation treatment produces the lowest rate of false reports overall\, thou
 gh errors\, when they occur\, are larger in magnitude.
URL:https://unimelb.zoom.us/j/82654401351?pwd=V6TMN2ZpNRILVKO2Y5za5S7GjfbAG
 G.1&from=addon
END:VEVENT
