SUMMARY:PhD Brown Bag Seminar – Pengyun CHen (University of Melbourne) 
 – Are Green Bonds Financially Distinct? Evidence from Time Varying Marke
 t Connectedness
LOCATION:Room 304\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3053
DESCRIPTION:Pengyun CHen: “Are Green Bonds Financially Distinct? Evidence
  from Time Varying Market Connectedness”\n\nGoogle Maps: https://maps.ap
 p.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nClimate change is a global negati
 ve externality that creates substantial demand for investment in the green
  transition. Green financial markets may support this process by reallocat
 ing capital toward low carbon activities\, but the financial role of green
  assets within the broader asset system remains unclear. This paper focuse
 s on green bonds as a financing based proxy for sustainable investment and
  examines whether they constitute a distinct segment of financial markets\
 , whether they behave as safe assets\, and whether their behaviour varies 
 across market conditions. Using the Diebold and Yilmaz (2009\, 2012\, 2014
 ) connectedness framework\, I construct time varying forecast error varian
 ce decomposition based spillover networks to analyse shock transmission be
 tween green bonds\, conventional assets\, market risk indicators\, and cli
 mate risk measures. The empirical framework allows green bonds to be class
 ified according to their role as shock receivers\, shock transmitters\, or
  partial safe assets within the financial system.
END:VEVENT
