SUMMARY:PhD Brown Bag Seminar – Abhirupa Das (University of Melbourne) 
 – Effect of Social Learning when Corruption “Greases the Wheels”: An
  Experimental Study
LOCATION:Room 304\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3053
DESCRIPTION:Abhirupa Das: “Effect of Social Learning when Corruption “G
 reases the Wheels”: An Experimental Study”\n\nGoogle Maps: https://map
 s.app.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nI propose a laboratory experi
 ment to empirically study how social learning and peer observability influ
 ence the evolution of bribe-setting behaviour among public service provide
 rs in a networked environment where bribes have certain welfare-enhancing 
 properties. Particularly\, the experiment would examine how exposure to pe
 ers' bribe-setting choices affects extortionary corruption\, and whether s
 uch exposure leads to norm convergence\, learning\, or crowding-in of unet
 hical behaviour. This study aims to contribute to the understanding of beh
 avioural mechanisms underlying corruption and has important implications f
 or institutional design\, especially where service delivery agents operate
  with high discretion and limited oversight.
END:VEVENT
