SUMMARY:PhD Brown Bag Seminar – Martina Repetto (University of Melbourne)
  – From Awareness to Action: Help-Seeking and Femicides after Gender-Bas
 ed Violence Campaigns in Italy
LOCATION:Room 304\, FBE Building\, 111 Barry St\, Carlton VIC 3053
DESCRIPTION:Martina Repetto: “From Awareness to Action: Help-Seeking and 
 Femicides after Gender-Based Violence Campaigns in Italy”\n\nGoogle Maps
 : https://maps.app.goo.gl/BirLkJKurX9pSbBB8\n\nABSTRACT:\nThis paper exami
 nes whether public awareness campaigns affect help-seeking behaviour and s
 evere violence outcomes in the context of gender-based violence (GBV). We 
 focus on the annual campaign surrounding the International Day for the Eli
 mination of Violence against Women (November 25)\, leveraging the unusuall
 y high level of public attention observed in Italy in 2023--2024. Using ad
 ministrative data on helpline calls and femicides\, we estimate a differen
 ce-in-differences model comparing outcomes before and after the campaign p
 eriod across years of varying intensity. We find that helpline calls incre
 ase by about 5 additional calls per week in an average-sized province foll
 owing the high-intensity campaign\, while femicides decrease by approximat
 ely 1 every four months in an average-sized region. Placebo tests and even
 t-study specifications support a causal interpretation. These findings sug
 gest that awareness campaigns may contribute to the prevention of severe f
 orms of gender-based violence.
END:VEVENT
